IMPORT prelude

-- Education Service Incentive Payment Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the CONNECT Plan for teachers: who the Plan must cover (s 3(1), with
-- the definitions of teaching service and teaching duties in s 2), who is paid the award when a member dies (s 3(2)), the
-- protection of awards and contributions from creditors and the Official Assignee (ss 6, 7), the Minister's power to withhold on
-- conviction or discipline (s 8), the award outside the member's estate (s 9), recovery of awards (s 10), what the Fund may pay
-- for (ss 12-14), its financial year (s 15(4)) and the offence of obstructing the auditor (s 16(6)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ESIPA2001.txt. The deposit says the revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The
-- latest amendment its Legislative History annotates is Act 40 of 2018 (Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018,
-- s 472, in force 30 July 2020), which touched s 7(2).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0170 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The person it applies to is a teacher in a Government or aided school.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The CONNECT Plan itself -- the award amounts, the prescribed period of qualifying service and the contribution
-- rates -- lives in regulations made under s 3, which are not deposited here; this Act sets only the frame. Also not encoded:
-- the Fund's receipts (s 11), the Minister's surplus-transfer judgement beyond its effect (s 13), accounts and audit
-- procedure (ss 15(1)-(3), 16(1)-(5), (7)-(10)), periodic actuarial examination (s 17) and rules (s 18).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Education Service Incentive Payment Act 2001 -- the CONNECT Plan`

§§ `2 -- teaching duties`

-- s 2: "'teaching duties' includes -- (a) the administration of any school; (b) the inspection or supervision of individuals
-- engaged in teaching duties in any school; and (c) other duties connected with the teaching or other services provided at any
-- school, being duties for the performance of which experience as a teacher is an advantage".
-- That classroom teaching is itself a teaching duty is an INFERENCE: the definition "includes" and does not list it.
DECLARE Duty IS ONE OF
    `classroom teaching`
    `administering a school`
    `inspecting or supervising teachers`
    `a school duty where teaching experience is an advantage`
    `a school duty where teaching experience is no advantage`

GIVEN `the duty` IS A Duty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty is a teaching duty` IF
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `a school duty where teaching experience is no advantage` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3(1) -- who the Plan must cover`

-- s 3(1): the Plan is for "(a) all public officers appointed ... to the PERMANENT ESTABLISHMENT in the Education Service and who
-- are BELOW SUPERSCALE grade; and (b) all individuals employed OTHER THAN FOR A TERM ... by the managers of any AIDED SCHOOL for
-- teaching duties, and who are remunerated on terms equivalent to any public officer mentioned in paragraph (a)".
-- s 2: an "aided school" and a "Government school" each EXCLUDE an independent school. "Teaching service" is service "whether
-- part-time or full-time", and s 3(1) says nothing of hours.
--
-- Paragraph (a) does not require teaching duties: any permanent public officer in the Education Service below Superscale is
-- covered. Paragraph (b) does not reach staff employed directly by an independent school, nor contract (term) staff of an aided
-- school.
DECLARE Employer IS ONE OF
    `the Government, in the Education Service`
    `the managers of an aided school`
    `an independent school`
    `a private school`

DECLARE Teacher HAS
    `employer` IS AN Employer
    `on the permanent establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `below Superscale grade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed for a term` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed for teaching duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `remunerated on terms equivalent to an eligible public officer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the teacher` IS A Teacher
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Plan must cover the teacher` IF
    CONSIDER `the teacher`'s `employer`
    WHEN `the Government, in the Education Service` THEN
            `the teacher`'s `on the permanent establishment`
        AND `the teacher`'s `below Superscale grade`
    WHEN `the managers of an aided school` THEN
            (NOT `the teacher`'s `employed for a term`)
        AND `the teacher`'s `employed for teaching duties`
        AND `the teacher`'s `remunerated on terms equivalent to an eligible public officer`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3(2) -- who is paid the award`

-- s 3(2): the regulations must provide for an award "(a) to a member of the CONNECT Plan; or (b) if the member dies before such
-- payment -- (i) to such of the member's dependants as the Minister thinks fit; or (ii) if the member has no dependants, to the
-- member's legal personal representative, on account of the member completing the prescribed period of qualifying service".
-- s 4: "No member has an absolute right to compensation for past service or to any award under the CONNECT Plan."
DECLARE Payee IS ONE OF
    `the member`
    `such of the member's dependants as the Minister thinks fit`
    `the member's legal personal representative`

GIVEN `the member is alive at payment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the member left dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Payee
`who is paid the award` MEANS
    IF `the member is alive at payment` THEN `the member`
    ELSE IF `the member left dependants` THEN `such of the member's dependants as the Minister thinks fit`
         ELSE `the member's legal personal representative`

§§ `6 -- creditors cannot reach the award`

-- s 6: no award, Government contribution or interest "is assignable or transferable, or liable to be garnished, attached,
-- sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or claim, other than -- (a) a debt due to the Government; or (b) an
-- order of court for the payment of PERIODICAL sums of money towards the maintenance of the WIFE or FORMER WIFE or MINOR CHILD
-- (whether legitimate or not) of the member".
--
-- The maintenance exception is for periodical sums only, and only for a wife, former wife or minor child: a lump-sum order, an
-- order for a husband and an order for an adult child are outside it. Whether the two exceptions also qualify "assignable or
-- transferable" is left open; this rule covers attachment only.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a wife`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a former wife`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a minor child born outside marriage`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a husband`
    `a periodical maintenance order for an adult child`
    `a lump-sum maintenance order for a former wife`
    `a bank loan`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the award may be attached for the claim` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a former wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a minor child born outside marriage` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- bankruptcy`

-- s 7(1): "No contribution by the Government made under the CONNECT Plan and no interest on the contribution (if any) is to be
-- subject to the debts of any member". (2): they do not "pass to the Official Assignee on the bankruptcy of a member" and are
-- "deemed excluded from the property of the bankrupt" for the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018.
--
-- s 7 names contributions and interest only. An award already paid to the member is not mentioned, so s 7 does not exclude it.
-- (Whether some other law does is not read.) s 7(1) has no exception for a debt due to the Government, while s 6(a) lets the
-- Government attach the same contribution: the two sit uneasily.
DECLARE Money IS ONE OF
    `a Government contribution`
    `interest on a Government contribution`
    `an award paid to the member`

GIVEN `the money` IS A Money
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 keeps the money from the Official Assignee` IF
    CONSIDER `the money`
    WHEN `an award paid to the member` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8 -- withholding on conviction or discipline`

-- s 8(1): the Minister may "withhold or refuse to pay (in whole or in part) any award" if, at the date of payment, the member --
-- "(a) has been convicted and SENTENCED TO DEATH OR ANY TERM OF IMPRISONMENT, by any court of competent jurisdiction, whether in
-- Singapore or ELSEWHERE, for any crime or offence and has not received a FREE PARDON; or (b) has been dismissed, reduced in rank
-- or CHARGED with any disciplinary charge for any negligence, irregularity or misconduct in the teaching service".
-- s 8(2): the same test, at the date a Government contribution is due, lets the Minister withhold the contribution.
--
-- A conviction punished by a fine alone does not open the power. A disciplinary CHARGE does, before any finding. The power is
-- discretionary ("It is lawful for the Minister to"), so this rule says only when it is open.
DECLARE Sentence IS ONE OF
    `no conviction`
    `a fine only`
    `a term of imprisonment`
    `death`

DECLARE `Member's record` HAS
    `sentence` IS A Sentence
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reduced in rank` IS A BOOLEAN
    `charged with a disciplinary charge for negligence, irregularity or misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sentence` IS A Sentence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is death or imprisonment` IF
    CONSIDER `the sentence`
    WHEN `a term of imprisonment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `death` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the record` IS A `Member's record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may withhold` IF
        (    `the sentence is death or imprisonment` (`the record`'s `sentence`)
         AND (NOT `the record`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `the record`'s `dismissed`
    OR  `the record`'s `reduced in rank`
    OR  `the record`'s `charged with a disciplinary charge for negligence, irregularity or misconduct`

§§ `9 -- the award and the deceased member's estate`

-- s 9: subject to the regulations, "all moneys paid or payable under the CONNECT Plan in respect of a deceased member are not to be
-- deemed to form part of his or her estate or be subject to the payment of his or her debts but are deemed to be property passing
-- on his or her death for the purposes of the Estate Duty Act 1929".
DECLARE `Estate question` IS ONE OF
    `forms part of the estate`
    `answers for the deceased's debts`
    `is property passing on death for estate duty`

GIVEN `the question` IS AN `Estate question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9 answers yes` IF
    CONSIDER `the question`
    WHEN `is property passing on death for estate duty` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10 -- recovering an award`

-- s 10: every award is paid on condition "that the Government may recover, cancel or reduce it if it is shown to have been obtained
-- by the WILFUL SUPPRESSION of material facts or to have been paid in IGNORANCE of facts which, had the facts been known before the
-- payment of that award to the member, would have justified the member's DISMISSAL from the teaching service or a REDUCTION OF THE
-- MEMBER'S SALARY".
-- Note s 8 speaks of reduction in RANK; s 10 of reduction of SALARY.
GIVEN `obtained by wilful suppression of material facts` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unknown facts would have justified dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unknown facts would have justified a salary reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may recover, cancel or reduce the award` IF
        `obtained by wilful suppression of material facts`
    OR  `unknown facts would have justified dismissal`
    OR  `unknown facts would have justified a salary reduction`

§ `Education Service Incentive Payment Act 2001 -- the CONNECT Fund`

§§ `12 to 14 -- what the Fund may pay for`

-- s 12: moneys "may ONLY be withdrawn and applied" for "(a) the payment of any award under the CONNECT Plan; (b) all expenses
-- incidental to or arising from the administration, investment and management of the Fund, including the cost of auditing the
-- accounts of the Fund; (c) any other purposes related to AIDED SCHOOLS OR GOVERNMENT SCHOOLS that may be prescribed by the
-- Minister by notification in the GAZETTE".
-- s 13: the Minister may by warrant transfer to the Consolidated Fund moneys which in the opinion of the Minister and the
-- Minister for Finance "are not immediately required". s 14(2): "A payment must not be made out of the Fund unless the payment is
-- authorised by the Minister."
--
-- Reading s 13 as a further permitted withdrawal beside s 12 is an INFERENCE (s 14(1) allows withdrawals "authorised or directed
-- ... under this Act"). An independent school is neither an aided nor a Government school (s 2), so a Gazetted purpose for one
-- falls outside s 12(c).
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `paying an award`
    `auditing the Fund`
    `investment and management expenses`
    `a Gazetted purpose related to Government or aided schools`
    `an un-Gazetted purpose related to Government schools`
    `a Gazetted purpose related to an independent school`
    `a surplus transfer to the Consolidated Fund by warrant`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is permitted` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `an un-Gazetted purpose related to Government schools` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Gazetted purpose related to an independent school` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payment out of the Fund is lawful` IF
    `the purpose is permitted` `the purpose` AND `authorised by the Minister`

§§ `15(4) -- the financial year`

-- s 15(4): "The financial year of the Fund begins on 1 April of each year and ends on 31 March of the succeeding year."
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year in which the Fund's financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `year` ELSE `year` MINUS 1

§§ `16(6) -- obstructing the auditor`

-- s 16(5): the auditor "may require ANY PERSON to provide ... any information in that person's possession or to which that person
-- has access which the auditor considers necessary". (6): "Any person who, WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE, fails to comply with any
-- requirement of the auditor under subsection (5) or who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the auditor ... shall be guilty of
-- an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000."
--
-- On the words, "without reasonable excuse" sits in the failure-to-comply limb only; the hindering limb has no excuse written into
-- it. This rule follows the words. No imprisonment is provided.
GIVEN `failed to comply with the auditor's requirement` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the auditor offence` IF
        (`failed to comply with the auditor's requirement` AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `otherwise hindered, obstructed or delayed the auditor`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the auditor offence` MEANS 1000
